@page "/"

<PageTitle> Snake </PageTitle>

<h1>Welcome to Mason and Sinahi's Snake Game</h1>

<p>
    This is a multiplayer online game built using Blazor and the network. It communicates with a game server to receive and display the state of the game world, including all snakes, walls, and powerups.
</p>

<h2>Design Decisions</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Color Coding:</strong> Each snake is assigned a base color and an outline color that is based on their PlayerID. </li>
    <li><strong>Mouse Powerup:</strong> Each player can collect desert mouse powerups to grow in size. </li>
    <li><strong>Drawing When Disconnected:</strong> When the player is not actively connected, the world is not drawn. </li>
</ul>

<h2>Features Implemented</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Opening page that indicates if it is ready to connect to the server. </li>
    <li>If there are issues connecting, a message is displayed on the canvas. </li>
    <li>Connect to a server by entering name, address, and port.</li>
    <li>Responsive to keyboard input (WASD only) to control snake direction.</li>
    <li>Disconnect button to manually exit the game server. </li>
</ul>

<p><em>Thanks for playing!</em></p>